# Everything here is re-fetchable. `lod2.py fetch` (or `build`) re-downloads
# the tiles; the OSM extracts re-fetch on demand. Between them they are ~1.6 GB,
# which does not belong in git.

# Source archives downloaded from the LoD2 ATOM feed (~743 MB)
*.zip
*.crdownload

# Cached CityGML tiles (~886 MB) and OSM extracts (~17 MB)
data/tiles/
data/osm/

# Reference photography and archival scans (~103 MB). Sources are documented
# in PLAN.md §3 — re-downloadable, and the Neues Museum plate volume alone is
# 97 MB.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.pdf

# Downloaded reference geometry — museum scans and the like. All re-downloadable
# from the URLs in 90_credits.md; the Nofretete OBJ alone is 845 MB.
reference/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

.DS_Store
